`any` is a type in TypeScript that represents any value, including values of any other type. It is used when the type of a value is not known or not important. Using `any` can disable type checking for a specific variable or expression.

`never` is a type in TypeScript that represents a value that will never occur. It is used to indicate that a function or branch of code will never be reached. For example, a function that always throws an error and never returns a value would have a return type of `never`.

